From d7b60e363bb41732e1d01c987e5d3da3770efd75 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ritesh Pandit <riteshp2001@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 19:20:58 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 122/140] feat(player): unify audiobook controls, add shared
 bookmarks, and fix script reloads

Shared audiobook and audio playback UI
- Replace the standalone audiobook player with the existing audio controls,
  shared seekbar/timers, speed sheet, playlist, up-next panel, and visualizers.
- Present book title, author/narrator, whole-book progress, file titles, and
  original-URI artwork. Fit portrait book covers without cropping and keep
  book queues in their established file order.
- Reuse the common playback speed range and host audiobook rewind and sleep
  timer settings in the standard player-sheet presentation.
- Route artwork/visualizer double taps through configured player gestures.
  Book-relative seeks can cross files while retaining the pause state.
- Add dedicated backward/forward seek controls beside play/pause, with live
  configured seek amounts, localized tooltips, accessible targets, and a
  scrollable control row for constrained widths. Remove the stale lazy
  seek-duration cache. Do not introduce a second add-bookmark button.

Persistent bookmarks across video, music, and audiobooks
- Keep the existing video bookmark/current-chapter controls and the audio
  bookmark control: tap opens the chapter/bookmark list; long press captures
  a named point at the playback timestamp before the editor is opened.
- Use one shared bookmark entity, DAO, editor, and add/rename/delete/seek flow.
  Capture the actually loaded media identity under the session lock so a
  queue transition cannot assign the outgoing timestamp to the next item.
- Merge custom points and book/native chapters for the displayed timeline
  and seekbar markers, while preserving native chapter data for automatic
  intro/credits behavior. Determine chapter selection by timestamp and keep
  differently named points even when they share a timestamp.
- Advance Room from version 23 to 24. Migrate existing audiobook bookmark
  IDs, titles, positions, creation times, and track references before
  removing the old table; retain cascading book-track ownership.

Audiobook text and localization
- Reuse the lyrics view for supplied embedded/local audiobook text without
  automatic online song lookup or translation. Include online-lookup policy
  in lyrics cache identity and hide unsupported online book-text controls.
- Add bookmark empty/error, audiobook-text empty, and seek-direction labels
  in the default resources and every existing translated locale.
- Update the README feature table to describe the shared playback behavior.

Frame navigation feedback
- Remove the large centered frame-seek overlay and place a signed frame
  delta beside the bottom frame counter instead.
- Show forward deltas in green and backward deltas in red for swipes,
  frame-step buttons, and slider changes. Fade feedback after 1.5 seconds
  once interaction/stepping settles, and hide it on play/pause.
- Preserve snapshot handling and constrain counter/timestamp layout.

Script disable/re-enable lifecycle (issue #679)
- Include the master script switch, selected Lua/JS filenames, and configured
  directory in native core identity, with applied script state owned by the
  process-wide playback session.
- Replace add-only runtime script loading with a debounced lifecycle-aware
  player recreation when the script selection changes. Rebuild the native
  runtime instead of leaving removed scripts alive or loading duplicates.
- Stage the current media/queue and restore position/pause through recreation;
  protect lifecycle teardown, notification re-entry, and replacement media
  requests from discarding the prepared source or retaining stale playback.
- Prevent direct mini-player launches from bypassing a required runtime
  refresh. Prune disabled cached scripts even when the configured document
  tree is unavailable, and serialize asset synchronization with initialization.
- Remove obsolete script-disable warnings that advised reopening the video.

Requested history change
- Remove b9f1aeb240bc7b7ba6fd5877b1bb9d4f83470f24 and its stream-aware
  auto-crop changes from master, while retaining the earlier #680 fixes.
- Preserve the pending bookmark and script-session work when resolving the
  overlapping playback-session shutdown block.

Validation and remaining gates
- Per standing instructions, validation was static only: focused editor
  diagnostics, source/reference and resource inspection, staged whitespace
  checks, and a refreshed source graph. No Android build, tests, emulator,
  device playback, or UI verification was run.
- Room 24 schema export/migration execution and runtime checks for playback
  restoration, script toggles, bookmarks, and responsive layouts remain
  required. Generated schemas and changelog files were not manually edited.

CI compilation follow-up (run 35229713407)
- Import kotlinx.coroutines.flow.first for the script runtime observer,
  resolving the missing extension and cascading lambda/phase errors.
- Explicitly call the top-level AnimatedVisibility for frame feedback inside
  the nested Box/Row layout, and remove its now-unused import.
